id: date/iso-week/0197
area: date
op: Temporal.PlainDate.prototype.weekOfYear
in: int:-1 int:1 int:1
out: value: f64:0x404A800000000000
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: Temporal.PlainDate's weekOfYear and yearOfWeek count the weeks of a negative ISO year with a division that truncates toward zero, so -0001-01-01 falls in week 52 rather than 53 of -2 and -0002-12-28 in week 1 of -1 rather than 53 of -2, where ISOWeekOfYear's weekday arithmetic is floored. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-6.5 (the Date area's record; the correspondence's row G2).
prov: ref:dateref@1
script: new Temporal.PlainDate(-1, 1, 1).weekOfYear
note: ISOWeekOfYear of the Temporal proposal, which the pinned edition does not hold (correspondence row G2)
since: 14

