id: date/month-day/0037
area: date
op: Temporal.PlainMonthDay.from, a year's leap day
in: int:2000000100 int:2 int:29 str:"reject"
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-vm: Temporal.PlainMonthDay.from reduces a year past 1e9 in magnitude to 1972 + year modulo 400 before it regulates the date, so February 29 is accepted, constrained or refused by the leap-ness of a different year, where it is regulated in the year given. Answered by Broiler.VM docs/javascript-shared-libraries/milestones/sjl-6-date.md, SJL-6.4 (JSD-0072; the correspondence's row G3).
prov: ref:dateref@1
script: Temporal.PlainMonthDay.from({ year: 2000000100, month: 2, day: 29 }, { overflow: "reject" }).toString()
note: the date is regulated in the year given, whose leap-ness decides it (correspondence row G3)
since: 14

